      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CLIMB ON TOP (1) is the horse to beat after winning at Broome, where he sat handy, took over before the turn and fought on to beat Great Edition by just under a length. He was an outside chance there but brings the strongest recent win, drops back to a suitable 1190m range and has a strong record around this distance. OCEAN OUTLAW (5) has the most compelling danger profile, having run second in a BM68+ at Mt Newman despite racing wide throughout, and his earlier Broome run had merit after a slow start. TEABISCUIT (8) has to turn around two plain provincial efforts, yet his record at this track and distance keeps him in the mix for a better showing. FAMEUX (3) backs up quickly after a slow-start fourth at Mingenew and has enough 1190m form to be treated as a genuine place hope with a winning rider back aboard. BONNY ROCK (6) won't be far away coming back to this company.",
